From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frida Hou <Frida-a@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:54:13 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [GDN] recover spec W=1: records outside the Mamba page (same
 block size)

With prefix caching the hybrid block size is derived from the Mamba page
size, so recover's record ring in the page (3,412,928 vs 3,268,608 B for
Qwen3.8 k=3) gave 1728- instead of 1600-token blocks and different cache-hit
granularity than the per-token path (RTX PRO 6000: 5184 vs 4800 hit tokens = 3 blocks
each). The scheduler's bookkeeping itself caches the same blocks for
num_speculative_blocks K vs 0 (new CPU test with the real Scheduler).

With W = 1 every step folds its records, so they now live in a per-layer
row buffer [max_num_seqs, ...] outside the KV cache (allocated at model init,
counted by the memory profile; R = num_spec + 1) and the page is
byte-identical to the per-token path's. W > 1 keeps the persistent ring in
the page. Kernels index records by spec row (RECORDS_BY_ROW) or by slot.

Tests: kernel bit-exactness for row and slot records; model-path and align
tests use row records for W = 1; tests/v1/core/test_mamba_recover_spec_caching.py
compares cached block sets and the turn-2 hit across modes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
